Your rules for this feature, as the builders will follow them (each one applies to every case like it, not just the example):
  1. Whenever an item or order is returned, the refund is the amount the customer actually paid for the returned items, which means the price after any discount code and the item's share of any basket-wide discount. It is never reduced by points. The amount is in whole rupees, and if the calculation leaves a fraction (for example when two of three items are returned) it is rounded down to a whole rupee, never up. Example: a ₹2,000 kurta bought with a 20% code is refunded ₹1,600, and a ₹1,000 item from a ₹3,000 basket with ₹300 off is refunded ₹900.
  2. Whenever a refund is paid, it goes back by the same method the customer paid with, and only the cash actually paid is refunded to that method. Example: Vikram returns his whole ₹2,000 order, which he paid with ₹1,500 cash by card plus ₹500 worth of points. His card gets ₹1,500.
  3. Whenever a customer returns an item that came with a free item in a 'buy X, get Y free' offer and keeps the free item, the returned item is refunded at what was paid for it, and the free item stays free and is not charged. Example: the ₹1,200 jacket is refunded at what was paid, and the ₹300 scarf stays free.
  4. Whenever a return brings an order's total below the free-delivery threshold, nothing changes about delivery charges. The customer keeps free delivery and gets only the item refund. Example: Anita spent ₹1,100, got free delivery above ₹1,000, and returns a ₹300 item.
  5. Whenever a refund is requested, the amount depends on delivery date, final-sale status and whether the goods arrived damaged. (a) Goods that did not arrive damaged: a request within 7 days of delivery gets a full refund of the item price. A request from day 8 through day 30 gets a half refund of the item price. A request after day 30 gets no refund. The shipping fee is never refunded. (b) Final-sale items that did not arrive damaged get no refund at any time. (c) Goods that arrived damaged, including final-sale ones: a request up to 90 days after delivery gets the full amount including the shipping fee, and a request after day 90 gets nothing. No other refund windows apply (not 5, 10 or 15 days).
  6. Whenever an order is cancelled before it ships, the customer is refunded the amount they actually paid for the items. Nothing is returned for points, because points are earned only on the amount paid and none were spent.
  7. Whenever an order is placed, it earns loyalty points only if the total of its items after the discount, not including shipping, is at least ₹500. When it qualifies, the order earns 1 point for every full ₹50 of the amount paid for the items after the discount, not including shipping. A sale discount (for example 40% Diwali) does not reduce this rate. Example: Neha's ₹1,000 item with a 10% code is paid at ₹900, so points are worked out on ₹900. Farhan's Diwali sale order earns points on the discounted items amount if that amount is at least ₹500.
  8. Whenever an item is returned, the points taken back are exactly the points that item earned. Example: Karan earned 100 points, and returning the item that earned 40 of them takes back 40 points.
  9. Whenever an order is returned after the points it earned have already been spent, the customer's points balance goes negative by the shortfall, and that negative balance is deducted from the points she earns next. The refund is still the full amount, calculated only from what she paid for the items, and is not reduced by the points.
  10. Whenever a refund returns points to a customer, they come back as ordinary points on the account, with no expiry rule applied to them. The product has no points-expiry rule, and points are only earned and returned.
  11. Whenever an order is returned, no status or membership level changes, because the product has no Gold status or any membership levels. Example: an ₹8,000 return that takes a customer's yearly spend from ₹54,000 to ₹46,000 changes no status. The only rules a return applies are those set for refunds, loyalty points and the sales summary.
